        "content": "The government has provided some sections for tax savings that are relevant for students:\r\nSection 80C:\r\nTax deduction up to ₹1.5 lakh on investments. ELSS (SIP), PPF, FD (5-year), NSC, insurance premium — all fall under this.\r\nExample: ₹3 lakh taxable income, invest ₹1.5 lakh in ELSS = taxable income ₹1.5 lakh = zero tax! (Under old regime).\r\nSection 80CCD:\r\nAdditional ₹50,000 deduction in NPS (National Pension Scheme). If you're doing long-term retirement planning, NPS + 80CCD = extra tax save. Total 80C + 80CCD = ₹2 lakh deduction.\r\nSection 80TTA/80TTB:\r\nDeduction up to ₹10,000 on savings account interest. For senior citizens, ₹50,000 on FD interest (80TTB). For students, savings interest is a small but useful deduction.\r\nExample: ₹15,000 interest earned on savings account. ₹10,000 exempt under 80TTA.\r\nTaxable interest = ₹5,000 only.\r\nSection 80GG:\r\nIf you live on rent and don't get HRA? Deduction up to ₹60,000/year (conditions apply). PG/Hostel rent is also covered. You need to fill Form 10BA.\r\nExample: ₹5,000/month rent = ₹60,000/year. ₹60,000 deduction under 80GG. Taxable income reduced.\r\nSection 80E:\r\nDeduction on education loan interest — no limit! You can claim for up to 8 years. When EMI starts, take deduction on the interest portion.\r\nExample: ₹8 lakh education loan at 9%. First year interest = ₹72,000. Full ₹72,000 deductible under 80E. Taxable income directly reduced by ₹72,000.",
