        "title": "ITR Filing — Why and How",
        "content": "ITR (Income Tax Return) is the form you fill to give the government details of your annual income and tax. Even if your income is below the taxable limit, filing ITR is beneficial.\r\n4 Reasons to File ITR Even with Zero Tax:\r\nTo claim tax refund — if TDS was deducted and your income isn't taxable, you'll get a refund. ₹2,000 TDS = ₹2,000 refund.\r\nFor loan approval — banks look at ITR. Home loan, car loan, personal loan — ITR = income proof.\r\nFor visa — foreign travel requires ITR proof. US, UK, Schengen — all ask for ITR.\r\nFor financial record — official income history. If you want to start a business in the future, ITR is useful.\r\nITR Filing Process — 7 Steps:\r\nStep 1: Go to incometax.gov.in (official website).\r\nStep 2: Register with PAN (already registered if you've done it before).\r\nStep 3: Select ITR-1 (for salary income) or ITR-2 (for capital gains).\r\nStep 4: Fill income details from Form 16.\r\nStep 5: Claim deductions under 80C, 80D, 80E etc.\r\nStep 6: Verify tax calculation — payable or refund.\r\nStep 7: Verify with Aadhaar OTP or digital signature. Submit!\r\nIt's free — simple salaried people don't need a CA. Time: 15-30 minutes.\r\nDeadline: July 31 of every year (for previous financial year). Late filing = ₹1,000-₹5,000 penalty.\r\nITR-1 vs ITR-2 vs ITR-3:\r\nITR-1 (Sahaj): Salary + one house property + other sources (interest). Most students/freshers.\r\nITR-2: Capital gains (SIP, stocks), multiple house property. If you've sold equity.\r\nITR-3: Business/profession income. Freelancers, business owners.\r\nITR-4 (Sugam): Presumptive income. Freelancers under 44ADA.\r\nCommon ITR Mistakes:\r\nSelecting the wrong ITR form.\r\nTDS mismatch — Form 16 vs Form 26AS.\r\nOverclaiming deductions — fake 80C receipts.\r\nNot declaring bank interest — AI will catch you.\r\nNot verifying — ITR was never actually filed!",
